# Merchant Dashboard – UI Implementation Rule

## Objective

Build the Merchant Dashboard UI for the Ashraf Courier Business Platform, strictly following the provided flowchart and design system.  
**No backend logic or API integration—focus is on layout, navigation, and user experience.**

---

## 1. Technology & Design System

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)
- **State Management:** Zustand (for client-side state, if needed)
- **Transitions:** Use premium, subtle transitions as per premium-transitions-and-effects.mdc
- **Accessibility:** All UI must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast)

---

## 2. Scope & Requirements

### Dashboard Features (All UI, No Backend)
- **Welcome Banner:** Personalized greeting, business name, and quick stats.
- **Quick Actions:** Prominent buttons for "Create New Shipment", "Track Package", "Analytics", etc.
- **Recent Shipments:** List or table of recent shipments (mock data), with status badges and action buttons.
- **Tracking Widget:** Enter tracking number to view status (mock).
- **Analytics Preview:** Mini chart or summary cards (mock data).
- **Notifications:** Section for recent alerts or updates (mock).
- **Navigation:** Sidebar or top nav for dashboard sections (Shipments, Analytics, Profile, etc.).
- **Profile/Account Menu:** Avatar with dropdown for account settings and logout (UI only).

---

## 3. Navigation

- Use Next.js App Router for all navigation.
- All flows must match the provided user flowchart.
- All navigation and state changes handled client-side (no server calls).

---

## 4. Data & Logic

- All data is static, mocked, or placeholder.
- No API calls, no backend logic, no authentication.
- Use mock data for lists, charts, and status updates.

---

## 5. Code Quality & Structure

- Use TypeScript everywhere.
- Functional components only.
- Early returns, no dead code, no TODOs.
- Descriptive naming and clear structure.
- All forms, buttons, and flows must be visually complete and accessible.

---

## 6. Deliverables

- Merchant Dashboard page and all required UI components.
- Fully navigable UI demo (no backend).
- README update with instructions for running the frontend demo.

---

## 7. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify adherence to this rule file and referenced standards.
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by the project lead.

---

**Goal:**  
Deliver a pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern Merchant Dashboard UI, ready for future backend/API integration.

---